# A common free cone on the fixed native occupation code

This finite construction keeps the native mass selector, its selected spectral
states, all native references, the complete sixteen-occupation code at each of
eight macrovertices, and the charge/Gauss representation of
`model/native_wilson_maxwell`. Its Hamiltonian contains an explicitly changed
Wilson regulator and a positive native-complement term. The result is a common
quadratic free fermion/photon cone, a unique active physical finite ground with
a certified gap, and a nonzero complete interaction record from an imperfect
native preparation. Neither an interacting relativistic limit nor an observed
particle assignment follows from these finite statements.

## Fixed source and explicit changed terms

Let `m` be precisely the positive native excitation selected by the maximal
positive elementary/Higgs cross residue in the parent's refined radius-two bin.
This is the parent's algebraic spectral value, with its retained rational
interval. Set `a=1/m`, `g=1/64`. There are 32 full native constituents, grouped
four per macrovertex, with global occupation-code projector `P=product P_x`.
Every constituent retains its old, dual, port and spin references. The fixed
canonical field `Psi`, the full density `rho`, and the integer-Gauss isometry
`Y` are literally the parent's operators. In particular, on the code,

`rho_x=Psi_x^dagger Psi_x-2`, `Q_total=sum rho_x`,

and outside it the full inherited density has range `[-4,4]`. No change of a
one-body spectral frame redefines these operators. The compensator has
`R=-Q_total`, retained labels `-32,...,32` and energy `4|R|`. The seven independent
longitudinal labels have range `-4,...,4`. All outer-constraint failures have the
same zero Hamiltonian extension. Native Gauss-violating states remain in the
kinematic carrier; physical ground statements concern the native physical
Gauss carrier. Zero-energy preparation-reference spectators are retained;
uniqueness counts the active factor rather than arbitrary spectator vectors.

Take the parent's Hermitian Clifford matrices `alpha_j,beta` and set

`Gamma=alpha_1 alpha_2 alpha_3 beta`.

The literal four-dimensional matrices satisfy `Gamma^2=I`, `Gamma†=Gamma`,
`{Gamma,beta}={Gamma,alpha_j}=0`. Gamma commutes with the three proper spin
rotation generators. On a graph of degree `d_x`, the one-body source is

`h_perp,xx=m beta+d_x Gamma/(2a)`,
`h_perp,tail head=-(Gamma+i alpha_j)/(2a)`.

The Hermitian conjugate is placed on the reversed edge. Relative to the
parent's beta regulator, the exact added onsite term is
`d_x(Gamma-beta)/(2a)` and the exact added directed bond is
`-(Gamma-beta)/(2a)`. They are second-quantized in the **fixed** Psi field and
guarded by the same global code. In the Peierls source they use precisely the
parent's finite transverse phase and longitudinal partial shifts. The raw code
scalar `-E_sea,beta` is retained. No subtraction of the perpendicular filled
sea is included. The separate declared term is

`H_complete=m c sum_x(I-P_x)`, `c=21/2`.

Thus the native complement has its native Hamiltonian, finite field, Coulomb
and reference energies, plus this stated positive term. Its kinetic and
current couplers vanish by the same global code guard. This architecture
supplies no all-state tensor-locality theorem on the full native carrier.

## Charge covariance and native implementation

For `K_e=Psi_head† B_e† Psi_tail`, with `B_e=-(Gamma+i alpha_j)/(2a)`,

`[rho_x,K_e]=D_ex K_e`, `D_e,tail=-1`, `D_e,head=+1`.

All 96 edge/site commutators are checked on the actual 32-dimensional matrix.
The code also executes a finite rational local gauge transformation. Every
spinor component has the same Abelian charge, and Gamma changes no charge
label. The positive phase multiplies `K_e exp(+ig Q_e)`, with the original
partial longitudinal shifts. Consequently the fixed Y intertwines this
Hamiltonian with the same physical Gauss carrier. The derivative current is
`J_phase=i(K_e-K_e†)`; charge flow is `I_flow=-J_phase`, so
`dot rho=D^T I_flow`. Finite transverse coordinates need not commute with one
another at their cutoff boundary for these charge identities to hold.

The native code consists of actual spectral states and their complete matrix
units. `support_control()` reexecutes the sixteen-occupation embedding, exact
port-charge intertwiner and shared-reference-vacuum intersection. The latter
is `P Q_all_Rloc_vac=|g^32,refvac><g^32,refvac|`. These are native spectral
services; their efficient compilation from a passive repair rule is not a
consequence of the matrix-unit definition.

Each `P_x` commutes with the native sum and port charge by spectral invariance.
The fixed parent frame acts within P and as identity outside P, hence commutes
with every `P_x`. So do its density, Coulomb, Y and every globally guarded
current term. The executed 81-state selected-port calculation and coherent
charge/Gauss lift check this pattern decomposition. Therefore the completion
is positive, reduces the full source, vanishes on P, and is at least `mc` on
its complement. Native/reference sectors are retained in this comparison.

## Free cone and finite-band calculation

On the translation-invariant comparison lattice, write
`w_j=1-cos(ap_j)`, `W=sum w_j` and
`Omega_gamma^2=2W/a^2`. The actual symbols obey

`h_perp=m beta+sum_j alpha_j sin(ap_j)/a+Gamma W/a`,
`E_perp^2-m^2=Omega_gamma^2+2 sum_(i<j) w_i w_j/a^2`.

The quadratic coefficients agree. On an axis the relation is exact. At fixed
positive m, `|E_perp-sqrt(m^2+|p|^2)|<=a^2|p|^4/(12m)`. The beta-regulated
parent instead has coefficient `1+ma`, equal to two at its `a=1/m`. Volume
increase alone does not remove that difference. The cone computation proves
these algebraic statements independently. Ordinary parity and time reversal
are broken by the perpendicular regulator at finite spacing; charge
conjugation and proper spin rotations are retained. This is a vectorlike
common-charge representation, without a Standard Model chirality claim.

For any finite Hermitian gauge background, write `h_perp=m beta+A`.
`{beta,A}=0`, so `h_perp^2=m^2+A^2>=m^2`. Functional calculus gives
`E=sqrt(m^2+A^2)` and the exact analysis frame

`F=(E+m+beta A)/sqrt(2E(E+m))`, `FF†=I`, `Fh_perp F†=beta E`.

This analysis does not change fixed Psi, rho or Y. On the actual open cube the
independent edge and Kronecker assemblies agree. The exact characteristic
polynomial of `h_perp/m` is

`(4z²-5)²(4z²-13)²(16z⁴-136z²+241)^4(16z⁴-264z²+977)²/2^32`.

Its positive energies are

| Energy divided by m | Multiplicity |
|---|---:|
| `sqrt(5)/2` | 2 |
| `sqrt(13)/2` | 2 |
| `sqrt(17-4sqrt(3))/2` | 4 |
| `sqrt(17+4sqrt(3))/2` | 4 |
| `sqrt(33-4sqrt(7))/2` | 2 |
| `sqrt(33+4sqrt(7))/2` | 2 |

All lie between one and four. The negative levels are their opposites.
The square-free degree-twelve annihilator is executed on the exact matrix.
No eigensolver supplies the certificate.

## Signed raw vacuum shift and full physical gap

Let `S_perp` be the sum of the sixteen positive energies divided by m in the
table, and `S_beta=4sqrt(3)+8sqrt(7)+4sqrt(13)`. The fixed scalar gives the
perpendicular code vacuum a **positive** raw shift

`Delta=m(S_beta-S_perp)`, `Delta/m=9.207886705480258...`.

With `E_base=32 E_g+m(3+sqrt(6))`, its free energy is `E_base+Delta`.
The original native complement has minimum `E_base+delta_native`, where the
unchanged constituent calculation certifies
`delta_native in [8.2075842638e-22,8.2103471906e-22]`. Charged ports and occupied
old/dual references have larger lower gaps. The perpendicular replacement
alone therefore places the physical ground in the native complement.
A normal-ordering convention cannot remove this comparison while retaining
the fixed raw source.

A rank-two partial-isometry bond has two independent hopping channels.
For a fixed eigenvalue q of a finite transverse coordinate, the complete
fermion Fock norm of its phase difference is
`2m|exp(igq)-1|<=2mg|q|`. The exact four-mode Fock control executes its
spectrum at a rational unit phase. Applying this bound to each edge, using
`||Q_e||<3/4`, and summing gives `||V_hop||<=18mg`. This proof requires no
commutation between different edge coordinates.

Let `R_0=I-e_root 1^T` and let G be the actual cube Green matrix. The exact
256-corner convex enumeration gives

`max_(rho in [-2,2]^8) rho^T R_0^T G R_0 rho/2=116/3`.

On the neutral code, `R_0 rho=rho` and `||G||=1/2`, giving the separate bound
8. On the full native physical charge box `[-4,4]^8`, the bound is `464/3`.
The reference energy `4|R|` is additional and nonnegative. Thus every code
charge sector obeys

`||V_hop+H_C||/m<=nu_all=18g+(116/3)g²=0.29069010416666...`.

The free code vacuum is unique, and its full free gap, including all reference
sectors, is at least `sqrt(5)m/2`. Min-max perturbation therefore gives a
unique interacting code ground with gap

`m[sqrt(5)/2-2nu_all] > m/2`.

Its energy relative to E_base is in `[Delta-m nu_all,Delta+m nu_all]`.
The code ground is neutral by charge conservation and the gap along the
continuous coupling path. No charged-sector norm is replaced by a neutral
estimate in this step.

If `Delta_U` is the outward upper shift divided by m, the minimal sufficient
completion coefficient is `Delta_U+nu_all`; its guaranteed separation may
be only the native gap. The explicit integer rule

`c=ceil(Delta_U+nu_all)+1/2=21/2`

gives complement separation at least
`delta_native+m[c-Delta_U-nu_all]>m/2`. Consequently the complete active
physical ground is in the code and

`gap_full >= min(m[sqrt(5)/2-2nu_all],`
`               delta_native+m[c-Delta_U-nu_all]) > m/2`.

The receipt evaluates all roots outward and reports both margins. A native
triplet outside one macrocell code saturates the native complement minimum;
all other retained native and reference states have nonnegative extra costs.
The unchanged full source zero on the outer Gauss-orthogonal extension does
not undercut this ground: `E_g in [8e_L-v,8e_U+v]` and the retained raw shift
show its raw energy is strictly negative. The finite gap has no
massless-photon infinite-volume interpretation.

## A prepared state in the fixed charge frame

The beta and perpendicular negative one-body projectors are P_beta and
P_perp. Exact rational matrix polynomial enclosures, with a stated uniform
sign-function remainder and entry-rounding norm bound, prove
`||P_perp-P_beta||<0.664<1`. Therefore

`V=[P_perp P_beta+(I-P_perp)(I-P_beta)]`
`    [I-(P_perp-P_beta)^2]^-1/2`

is a unitary direct rotation mapping the parent filled sea to the perpendicular
filled sea. Its ordinary number-preserving second quantization in fixed Psi
commutes with total charge. The universal two-projection calculation verifies
`S†S=SS†=I-(P_perp-P_beta)^2`, `S P_beta=P_perp S`, and commutation of
the positive square with both projectors and S. Extend the lifted rotation as identity on the native code
complement and lift by the unchanged Y. This is a declared physical finite
unitary; it supplies no redefinition of local density. Its construction
requires exact algebraic spectral services, without a claim of an efficient
native gate implementation.

Compose this unitary with the parent's actual deterministic 32-constituent
trial preparation. No initial code or ground measurement is inserted. The
complete state has code weight at least the parent's certified `p_code`, and
its code component is exactly the perpendicular free sea times photon vacuum.
The complement is retained. Every added local reference is vacuum on that
trial support, and the original spin references remain. The source and final
counts reduce the code, so any code outcome has actual probability equal to
the exact code weight times its ideal probability. The complement evolves
with its complete changed raw Hamiltonian.

## Fresh vacuum and complete finite records

Charge conjugation satisfies `C h_perp* C†=-h_perp` and
`C J_phase,e* C†=J_phase,e`. With `Tr J_e=0`, all current means vanish.
Its local action also gives `Tr(P_perp P_x)=2`, hence zero mean density.
The complete CAR Wick contraction is

`sigma²/m²=sum_(ef) (P4/4+P6/(2sqrt(6)))_ef`
`                    Tr(P_perp J_e(I-P_perp)J_f)`.

The exact rational-polynomial projector certificate gives
`1.3056143698852 < sigma²/m² < 1.3056201571726` and the fresh Coulomb vacuum
coefficient in `[0.3207282107617,0.3207297647557]`. The sign error is bounded
before entry rounding; Hilbert-Schmidt trace bounds propagate the resulting
projector error through every contraction. Binary64 values in the receipt
are diagnostic renderings of rational outward intervals.

Use the perpendicular positive/negative bands for particle/hole counts.
Their cardinality agrees with the parent, but their projectors differ. In the
neutral experiment, let `tau=mT=1/64` and retain the conservative bound
`nu_neutral=18g+59g²/4`, which exceeds `18g+8g²`. The first linear current
insertion is entirely in the one-particle, one-hole, one-photon subspace.
Every such free excitation has energy below `11m`. Its target amplitude is
at least `g tau sigma_L(1-11tau/2)`, where
`sigma_L` is a lower bound on the dimensionless norm `||V_1 vacuum||/m`. Photon parity removes the even part of
one insertion from that target. The odd Taylor remainder is at most
`(27/16)tau g³`; the complete second Duhamel remainder is
`tau² nu_neutral²/2`. Thus

`a_target=g tau sigma_L(1-11tau/2)`
`          -(27/16)tau g³-tau² nu_neutral²/2 >0`.

The original-attempt target probability is at least `p_code a_target²` and
the connected binary covariance at least
`p_code[a_target²-(tau nu_neutral)^4]>0`. The complement has no photon
excitation on its prepared neutral reference-vacuum support. Counts retain
all `(N_particle,N_hole,N_photon)` with `0,...,16`, `0,...,16`, `0,...,3`,
all four native-complement photon labels and the outer-constraint failure:
1161 labels in total. Their projectors sum to the full kinematic identity.
These are nonstationary prepared-free-vacuum dressing records. The interacting
ground existence theorem does not turn this input into that ground.

## Clock, control and full raw resources

A single duration-one preparation pulse composes all trial preparations and
the stated sea rotation. A duration-one readout records the full count
instrument and retains its final common source evolution. Between them the
same autonomous Hamiltonian acts for `T=1/(64m)`. Every branch has elapsed
source time `2+1/(64m)`.

Both pulses are explicit finite logarithm controls, `iLog(U)-H_ext`, with
principal eigenphases and full background cancellation. The readout chooses
`U=exp(-iH_ext) U_count`; its record refers to the interval start. The same
finite controller assumption as the parent is retained. It is not derived
from the primitive repair rule or from the Clifford algebra calculation.

The code replacement norm is below `139m`: the perpendicular second-quantized
matrix has norm below `64m`, the fixed sea scalar has magnitude below `43m`,
and the subtracted native code excitation operator is bounded by `32m`.
Using the larger bound `160m`, photon energy below `13m`, complete native
Coulomb bound `464mg²/3`, reference bound 128 and completion bound `8mc` gives

`B=32(600+360*2^-34)+m_U(173+18g+464g²/3+8c)+128`.

This is a raw norm bound without discarding native ground constants. Each
control norm is at most `B+pi`; absolute net bare-source work is at most `2B`
and gross two-pulse switching work at most `4(B+pi)`. The retained source,
reference, trial, field and count-pointer capacity is precisely the parent
formula, recorded in the result. Coefficient/synthesis workspace is an
additional controller resource and is not included in that capacity.

All changed onsite, bond and complement terms are explicit architecture
choices. The finite certificate proves no physical GeV scale, Standard Model
identification, weak chirality, interacting Lorentz limit, continuum field
limit or removal of the finite photon commutator boundary.
